{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 43, :comments ["<b>ונטמתם בם.</b> Defective alef, like <b>מחטו לי עגלות צב</b>, <b>מרשית השנה לא יהל שם ערבי</b>, <b>ותזרני חיל למלחמה</b>. And one may say that it is from the root <b>ונטמינו בעיניכם</b>, meaning like a person who lacks understanding."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The first interpretation cites biblical verses with defective alef forms where the triconsonantal root is spelled with only two radicals; the specific verse references (drawn from Psalms, Isaiah, and Joel) are presented as Chizkuni wrote them, without normalization."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:11:34.529548892Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}